# The function generates signals for a trading strategy based on trend following with a volatility filter.
# The moving average (SMA) with a window of 25 is used to determine the base signal as when close is above or below the SMA.
# The volatility (VOL) is calculated using the standard deviation of the one-bar returns of the last 40 bars.
# The position is set to 1 (long) when the close is above the SMA and the volatility is below a threshold, -1 (short) when the close is below the SMA and the volatility is below the threshold, and 0 (flat) otherwise.
# The strategy is allowed to have both long and short positions, and flat when both the moving average and volatility are not yet defined.
# Each bar is decided on its own, with no memory of earlier positions.

